  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Monday)\nIssued at 156 PM CDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\nAnother difficulty in messaging this rain event may be the\nperception that because the watch exists through Friday morning,\nit will be raining almost continuously through Friday morning. \nThis is not the case. Models are consistently showing that there \nwill be several rain events, mostly occurring during the overnight\nhours. A lack of rainfall during the day may seem as though the \nthreat has been exaggerated. However storm total rainfall amounts \nfrom several ensemble models indicate a swath of potential for \n1-2\" rainfall and even an outlier possibility of up to 5\". For our\nCWA those rainfall totals warrant a watch for the threat of \nflooding. \n\nThe rain is the headline grabber but that is not the only weather\ninterest this week. A strong cold front arrives Friday bringing\nour first real taste of fall as many areas fail to break 60\ndegrees for highs! That followed by lows in the 40s will bring a\nchill not seen since the spring to TX/SE NM. In addition, windy\nconditions behind the front will make Friday a brisk day to be\noutdoors. So go into the cabinet and dust off those chili, chicken \nsoup, and caldo recipes...they will be needed. At least for a \ncouple of days before warmer weather returns early next week.\n\nHennig",
